{
  "audio_file": "group_8_pair_1_statement1.wav",
  "duration": 74.04,
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 6.88,
      "duration": 6.88,
      "text": "these components and concepts come together in a complete agent workflow. A goal arrives."
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "start": 7.44,
      "end": 14.44,
      "duration": 7.0,
      "text": "The agent perceives it, adds it to context, and begins reasoning. It identifies the first action"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "start": 14.44,
      "end": 20.82,
      "duration": 6.38,
      "text": "needed and executes. The results come back. The agent evaluates whether it's closer to the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "start": 20.82,
      "end": 29.9,
      "duration": 9.08,
      "text": "It plans the next action. It executes again. This continues. Perceive, reason, act until the goal"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "start": 29.9,
      "end": 35.96,
      "duration": 6.06,
      "text": "is reached, an error condition is triggered, or the agent determines it cannot proceed and hands"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "start": 35.96,
      "end": 45.8,
      "duration": 9.84,
      "text": "off to a human. What's important to notice is that workflow is the handoff point. Good agent design"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "start": 45.8,
      "end": 52.06,
      "duration": 6.26,
      "text": "always includes a point at which the agent recognizes the limits of its confidence and"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "start": 52.06,
      "end": 60.64,
      "duration": 8.58,
      "text": "escalates. That's not a failure. It's responsible architecture. At Solara, an agent that flags an"
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "start": 60.64,
      "end": 67.14,
      "duration": 6.5,
      "text": "equipment anomaly it can't fully explain and routes it to a human engineer isn't falling short. It's"
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "start": 67.14,
      "end": 73.78,
      "duration": 6.64,
      "text": "doing exactly what it should. Let's bring it together. Every agent is built from four components."
    }
  ],
